{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5458) to create `cmd/fmt/main.go` — a contract/stub implementation for the GNU `fmt` text formatting utility. The task requires:\n   - Creating `cmd/fmt/main.go` with a complete program skeleton per srd070-fmt\n   - Calling `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - Parsing all SRD-defined flags: `-w` (width), `-g` (goal), `-s` (split-only), `-t` (tagged-paragraph), `-p` (prefix), `-u` (uniform-spacing)\n   - Defining function stubs with TODO bodies that print \"not implemented\" and exit 1 for all major operations: paragraph detection, line filling/wrapping, crown-margin handling, tagged-paragraph handling, prefix filtering, and uniform spacing\n   - The contract must compile but is NOT expected to produce correct output\n   - Acceptance criteria: AC1 (compiles), AC2 (all SRD flags parsed), AC3 (function stubs exist), AC4 (go vet passes)\n   - Git is managed externally — NO git commands allowed\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go unix utility pattern: copyright header, package doc comment, sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler(), manual flag parsing with os.Args\n   - SRD-driven development: implement only what the SRD specifies\n   - Contract/stub pattern: compilable skeleton with TODO stubs\n   - Differential testing against GNU reference binary (gfmt via Homebrew)\n   - SIGPIPE handling protocol for all cmd/ utilities\n   - Non-goals enforcement (E6): SRD non_goals says `-c` crown margin is NOT implemented beyond default indentation behavior\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max per function (E8)\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max (E9)\n   - No git commands — orchestrator manages git externally\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd070-fmt.yaml` (READ)\n     - Full SRD for fmt utility. Key requirements:\n       - R1: Default 75-char width formatting\n       - R2: Blank lines as paragraph separators\n       - R3: Indentation preservation (first line indent, subsequent lines match second line)\n       - R4: File/stdin input (files from args, stdin when no args or \"-\")\n       - R5: `-w WIDTH` / `--width=WIDTH` (default 75)\n       - R6: `-g GOAL` / `--goal=GOAL` (default 93% of width)\n       - R7: Word boundary breaking\n       - R8: Space collapsing (2 spaces after sentence-ending punctuation . ! ?)\n       - R9: `-s` / `--split-only` (split long lines, don't join short ones)\n       - R10: `-u` / `--uniform-spacing`\n       - R11: `-p PREFIX` / `--prefix=PREFIX` (reformat only prefixed lines)\n       - R12: `-t` / `--tagged-paragraph`\n       - R13: Exit codes (0=success, 1=error) and differential testing\n       - non_goals: NO crown margin mode (-c) beyond default; NO locale-aware line breaking\n\n   - `cmd/cat/main.go` (READ - reference pattern)\n     - Shows the standard cmd/ utility pattern used throughout the project:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // cmd/cat implements srd006-cat: ...\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"bufio\"\n         \"errors\"\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"io\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"syscall\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         args := parseFlags(os.Args[1:])\n         if len(args) == 0 {\n             args = []string{\"-\"}\n         }\n         // ... process files with exit code tracking\n     }\n     ```\n     - Uses manual os.Args flag parsing (not flag package)\n     - Global flag variables\n     - parseFlags returns file arguments after consuming flag arguments\n     - Error formatting helper `formatEr